pt09 adversarial lane, surface: misreading-firing contract. Greens the RED
frozen in the previous commit.

The v2.5.0 distinctive-token guard is the thing that stops a CORRECT
restatement from reading Contradicts: misreading-share alone is topic
evidence, so at least one shared token must be absent from the entry's own
affirmative voice before the branch will say the source asserts the rejected
reading. That voice was title + aliases + synopsis + boundary conditions.
`pressureTests` was left out — not by judgment but because it is not a
MATCH_SURFACE: it feeds no retrieval text and no score, so it had never
needed a token set.

Repro: "The Conversion Ladder separates exposure, attention, attraction, and
selection." read lexicon:term-conversion-ladder Contradicts at 0.881. That
entry's misreading CONFLATES the rungs the passage separates. The lone
distinctive hit was `selection` — a word the synopsis spells "chosen" and the
entry's own pressure test spells "selection". Now Resembles; score unchanged
at 0.881, as it must be.

Blast radius, measured over the 677 authored misreadings in the index: no
misreading loses its last distinctive token (5 have none either way), 38 lose
some and keep at least one. Corpus stance census over all 42 archived
sources: 0 of 1,298 displayed labels move and no score moves — which is also
the finding, because it means the archived corpus cannot see this class at
all. It is reachable only by a passage that restates an entry in vocabulary
the entry uses everywhere except its synopsis.

All 18 suite steps green. No floor moves: nothing here reaches a score, so
domainRecall, ignorePrecision, junkRecall, knownSplits and the weak backlog
are untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 js/lab-analyzer.js | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/js/lab-analyzer.js b/js/lab-analyzer.js
index 1b09c8a..9c078a8 100644
--- a/js/lab-analyzer.js
+++ b/js/lab-analyzer.js
@@ -1385,12 +1385,28 @@ function normalizeEntry(raw, index) {
    * token absent from every affirmative surface can evidence the misreading
    * as opposed to the claim. A misreading with no such token (4 of 588 at the
    * freeze) cannot be detected by this branch at all until it is authored one.
+   *
+   * `pressureTests` joins that affirmative voice at v2.6.x-opus-pt09 (pt09
+   * adversarial lane). It is authored canon prose about the entry's own claim,
+   * written in the entry's own vocabulary; it was omitted here only because it
+   * is not a MATCH_SURFACE — it feeds no retrieval text and no score, so it had
+   * never needed a token set. Leaving it out left the guard one-sided: a word
+   * the synopsis happens to spell differently ("chosen") but the pressure test
+   * spells plainly ("selection") counted as evidence of the rejected reading,
+   * so "The Conversion Ladder separates exposure, attention, attraction, and
+   * selection." — the concept restated correctly — read Contradicts at 0.881
+   * against lexicon:term-conversion-ladder, whose misreading CONFLATES the
+   * rungs the passage separates. Measured over the 677 authored misreadings in
+   * the index: no misreading loses its last distinctive token (5 have none
+   * either way), 38 lose some and keep at least one. Labels can move; scores
+   * cannot, because nothing here reaches the score.
    */
   const affirmativeSurfaceTokens = new Set([
     ...entry._surfaceTokens.title,
     ...entry._surfaceTokens.alias,
     ...entry._surfaceTokens.synopsis,
     ...entry._surfaceTokens.boundaryCondition,
+    ...tokenize(entry.pressureTests.join(' ')),
   ]);
   entry._misreadingDistinctiveSets = entry._misreadingTokenSets
     .map((tokens) => tokens.filter((token) => !affirmativeSurfaceTokens.has(token)));
